{"id":"CVE-2010-1634","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-05-27T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T01:28:41.542Z","description":"Multiple integer overflows in audioop.c in the audioop module in Python 2.6, 2.7, 3.1, and 3.2 allow context-dependent attackers to cause a denial of service (application crash) via a large fragment, as demonstrated by a call to audioop.lin2lin with a long string in the first argument, leading to a buffer overflow.  NOTE: this vulnerability exists because of an incorrect fix for CVE-2008-3143.5.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://bugs.python.org/issue8674","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/43068","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"43068"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2010-June/042751.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2010-9652"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/51087","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"51087"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2011/0212","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2011-0212"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-1616-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-1616-1"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/51040","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"51040"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/1448","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-1448"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/50858","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"50858"},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/Security-announce/2011//Oct/msg00003.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2011-10-12-3"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2011/0122","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"A