{"id":"CVE-2010-2089","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2010-05-27T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T02:17:14.558Z","description":"The audioop module in Python 2.7 and 3.2 does not verify the relationships between size arguments and byte string lengths, which allows context-dependent attackers to cause a denial of service (memory corruption and application crash) via crafted arguments, as demonstrated by a call to audioop.reverse with a one-byte string, a different vulnerability than CVE-2010-1634.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=598197","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/43068","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"43068"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2010-June/042751.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2010-9652"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/51087","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"51087"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2011/0212","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2011-0212"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-1616-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-1616-1"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/51040","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"51040"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/1448","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-1448"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/50858","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"50858"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/40863","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"40863"},{"url":"http://bugs.python.org/issue7673","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/Security-announce/2011//Oct/msg00003.html","tags":["vendor-advi