{"id":"CVE-2010-3492","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2010-10-19T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T03:11:44.327Z","description":"The asyncore module in Python before 3.2 does not properly handle unsuccessful calls to the accept function, and does not have accompanying documentation describing how daemon applications should handle unsuccessful calls to the accept function, which makes it easier for remote attackers to conduct denial of service attacks that terminate these applications via network connections.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/09/11/2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100910 Re: CVE Request -- Python -- accept() implementation in async core is broken => more subcases"},{"url":"http://bugs.python.org/issue6706","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2010:216","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2010:216"},{"url":"https://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A12111","tags":["vdb-entry","signature","x_refsource_OVAL"],"name":"oval:org.mitre.oval:def:12111"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/09/24/3","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100924 Re: CVE Request -- Python -- accept() implementation in async core is broken => more subcases"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/09/22/3","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100922 Re: CVE Request -- Python -- accept() implementation in async core is broken => more subcases"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/09/09/6","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100909 CVE Request -- Python -- accept() implementation in async core is broken => more subcases"},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2010:215","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2010:215"}],"vendors":["python"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-3493","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2010-10-19T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T03:11:44.427Z","description":"Multiple race conditions in smtpd.py in the smtpd module in Python 2.6, 2.7, 3.1, and 3.2 alpha allow remote attackers to cause a denial of service (daemon outage) by establishing and then immediately closing a TCP connection, leading to the accept function having an unexpected return value of None, an unexpected value of None for the address, or an ECONNABORTED, EAGAIN, or EWOULDBLOCK error, or the getpeername function having an ENOTCONN error, a related issue to CVE-2010-3492.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://svn.python.org/view/python/branches/py3k/Lib/smtpd.py?r1=84289&r2=84288&pathrev=84289","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/09/11/2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100910 Re: CVE Request -- Python -- accept() implementation in async core is broken => more subcases"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=632200","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/43068","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"43068"},{"url":"https://bugs.launchpad.net/zodb/+bug/135108","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2011/0212","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2011-0212"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/51040","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"51040"},{"url":"https://oval.cisecurity.org/repository/search/definition/oval%3Aorg.mitre.oval%3Adef%3A12210","tags":["vdb-entry","signature","x_refsource_OVAL"],"name":"oval:org.mitre.oval:def:12210"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/50858","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"50858"},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security